s digit with the ones column.\n\n```\n    15\n  \u00d7 49\n  135\n```\n\n3. **Multiply 15 by 4 (the tens digit of 49)**:\n   - Since 4 is in the tens place, we need to shift the result one place to the left. So, multiply 15 by 40 (which is the same as 15 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 10).\n   - Multiply 15 by 4: \\( 15 \\times 4 = 60 \\).\n   - Shift the result one place to the left: \\( 600 \\).\n\n```\n    15\n  \u00d7 49\n  135\n+ 600\n```\n\n4. **Add the two results together**:\n   - Add 135 and 600: \\( 135 + 600 = 735 \\).\n\n```\n    15\n  \u00d7 49\n  135\n+ 600\n-----\n  735\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 15 and 49 is 735. This confirms our previous answers using the distributive property method and the standard multiplication method.\n\nTo summarize, the product of 15 and 49 is \\(\\boxed{735}\\).\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, the product of 15 and 49, using the long multiplication method, is 735.</answer>",
