 equation \\( 75x + 60 = 30x - 200 \\) for \\( x \\), we need to isolate \\( x \\) on one side of the equation. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. **Subtract \\( 30x \\) from both sides** to get all \\( x \\)-terms on one side:\n   \\[\n   75x + 60 - 30x = 30x - 200 - 30x\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   45x + 60 = -200\n   \\]\n\n2. **Subtract 60 from both sides** to eliminate the constant term on the left side:\n   \\[\n   45x + 60 - 60 = -200 - 60\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   45x = -260\n   \\]\n\n3. **Divide both sides by 45** to isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{45x}{45} = \\frac{-260}{45}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   x = -\\frac{260}{45} = -\\frac{52}{9}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation \\( 75x + 60 = 30x - 200 \\) is \\( x = -\\frac{52}{9} \\).\n\n<answer>. The solution to the equation \\( 75x + 60 = 30x - 200 \\) is \\( x = -\\frac{52}{9} \\).</answer>.<|User|>Solve the equation 80x + 70 = 40x - 140 for x.\nPlease reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the equation \\( 80x + 70 = 40x - 140 \\) for \\( x \\), we need to isolate \\( x \\) on one side of the equation. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. **Subtract \\( 40x \\) from both sides** to get all \\( x \\)-terms on one side:\n   \\[\n   80x + 70 - 40x = 40x - 140 - 40x\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   40x + 70 = -140\n   \\]\n\n2. **Subtract 70 from both sides** to eliminate the constant term on the left side:\n   \\[\n   40x + 70 - 70 = -140 - 70\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   40x = -210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Divide both sides by 40** to isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{40x}{40} = \\frac{-210}{40}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   x = -\\frac{210}{40} = -\\frac{21}{4}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation \\( 80x + 70 = 40x - 140 \\) is \\( x = -\\frac{21}{4} \\).\n\n<answer>. The solution to the equation \\( 80x + 70 = 40x - 140 