be broken down into \\(100 - 1\\).\n   - \\(81\\) can be broken down into \\(80 + 1\\).\n\n2. **Draw a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles:**\n   - One rectangle will represent \\(100 \\times 80\\).\n   - Another rectangle will represent \\(100 \\times 1\\).\n   - The third rectangle will represent \\(-1 \\times 80\\).\n   - The fourth rectangle will represent \\(-1 \\times 1\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:**\n   - The area of the first rectangle (100 \u00d7 80) is:\n     \\[\n     100 \\times 80 = 8000\n     \\]\n   - The area of the second rectangle (100 \u00d7 1) is:\n     \\[\n     100 \\times 1 = 100\n     \\]\n   - The area of the third rectangle (-1 \u00d7 80) is:\n     \\[\n     -1 \\times 80 = -80\n     \\]\n   - The area of the fourth rectangle (-1 \u00d7 1) is:\n     \\[\n     -1 \\times 1 = -1\n     \\]\n\n4. **Add the areas of all the smaller rectangles:**\n   \\[\n   8000 + 100 - 80 - 1 = 8019\n   \\]\n\nSo, using the area model method, the product of \\(99 \\times 81\\) is \\(8019\\).\n\nThis method helps to visualize the multiplication and can be particularly useful for understanding the distributive property of multiplication. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8019}\n\\]",
